## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle): **1184 C F4 work-roll
IR under a round-roll setup model**.

- Trigger: delayed roll-change leaves a visual-PASS 0-spall; 11 min of
  hold writes a 38 mm circumferential spall and 1184 C F4 IR; setup
  model stays 912 C.
- Base rate: <1% — 0.38%/campaign from a work-roll MC (chatter-spec
  designed; spall fitted-style).
- Naive failure: FALSE PERMISSION. PB-FM-7 sees PYRO 912 C, LOOP
  8.4 kN, GAGE 1.82, raises, ships a cobble-plus-fire, $4.72M.
- Trajectory edit: put the spall in `state.fault_context`, make the
  round-roll setup model the mechanism that keeps all three confirms
  green, and force the gate to refuse the raise on r_spall 1184 even
  though all three playbook confirms are numerically true.

Distinct from the domain injection: the domain is the hot-strip finishing
train; the tail is the accidental model-nullspace compound.

## Neuromorphic Translator

Race window [6.746, 7.246] ms = 500 us. Winner spall.ir @ 6.818 ms
(amplitude 1.26, 1184 C). Loser pyro.in_band @ 7.010 ms (amplitude
1.09, 912 C). Margin 192 us vs combined jitter 62 us (3.10x).
shape.xray @ 7.154 ms is a third race-window channel. Gate @ 7.518 ms
= winner + 700 us.

Flip narrative: 192 us < min(500, 500) us, so order is flip-fragile. If
pyro-in-band wins, PB-FM-7 heads the triage queue. The hold must ride
order-invariant floors (r_spall, r_shape), not the winner tag.

