## Generator

Cycle-1 output is the base. Additive expansion (nothing removed):

1. Downstream side-effect (immediate): mill-pace probe at +6.4 s
   jumps F4 IR (19.4 K in 2.2 s, spall band >= 18) — spall, not noise.
   F4 isolate r_spall 1184 -> 908. Delay-table ridge inventory
   discovered during the isolate.
2. Delayed side-effect (PRIMARY terminal, not a footnote): at +8.6 min,
   delay-table bar cobbles at F1; $2.16M. The 11 min pre-t0 spall is
   the mechanism. Correct gate, campaign still misses.
3. Deepened `proposed_action.evidence` with units: r_spall 1184 C,
   r_shape 2.41 mm, PYRO 912 C, LOOP 8.4 kN, GAGE 1.82 mm, race 192 us.
4. Tightened rationale to the numeric floor no raise while r_spall >
   1020 C AND r_shape > 1.95 mm, plus probe bands >=18 vs <=3 K, plus
   HITL 8.8 min roll-change-interlock LOTO rule.

Reward retargeted to total -0.16 so the delayed miss is the inflection
(t_us 516000000), not the gate. Process heads remain non-zero.

## Critic

Re-audit of the expanded trajectory:

1. **blocking if unfixed — missing second domain constraint.** Production
   1.82 mm probe 6.4 s / -8% is not a universal number. A 0.8 mm
   thin-gauge campaign will buckle. Diversity Enforcer must inject the
   physical-constraints sub-variant this cycle.
2. **major — only one tail class.** Work-roll spall is accidental
   infrastructure. A disjoint human-intent tail is still required
   (Sunday-night F4-IR CSV forgery is the open cell).
3. **major — scar is still one edge in the cycle-1 raster.** NOTES-r14
   item 4 is not discharged until three raise-go edges exist and
   any-pair rollback is shown to fail at threshold 0.30.
4. **minor — contrast episode missing.** Without a same-gate ACCEPT on
   a true round-roll the record teaches "never raise". Add +4 d
   sister-mill contrast with its own race.
5. **minor — HITL latency mentioned in prose only.** Put 8.8 min in
   executed_action.parameters.human_ratify and in a tick.

No rewrite; directives only.

