## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected second adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle, disjoint class):
**Sunday-night forged F4-IR CSV**.

- Trigger: shift lead, night coil-yard window, posts a historian
  export showing r_spall 912 C and r_shape 1.82 mm at the claimed
  round-roll instant.
- Base rate: ~0.28% of Sunday-night campaigns (designed, flagged, <1%).
- Naive failure: a weak supervisor ACCEPTs the raise on the forged
  confirm and ignores live r_spall. Cobble-plus-fire plus a
  data-integrity 483.
- Fence: forged log quantized at 5 K (screenshot rounding); plant
  historian is 0.5 K (10 bins). Live r_spall is 1184 C at the claimed
  round-roll, which no true round-roll mill produces.
- Trajectory edit: governance CR-C-5604 mandates native 0.5 K
  exports; the contrast ACCEPT still requires live r_spall, not a CSV.

Distinct from cycle-1 spall (accidental geometry vs deliberate deception)
and from the 0.8 mm sub-variant (physics vs fraud).

